    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Did you have trouble staying seated in class when you were a child?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, oh my gosh, all the time. Even in elementary school, I was always the kid who couldn't stay in my seat. I'd be up wandering around the room, looking at the posters or whatever. And I was always talking over the teacher, just blurting things out before she even finished her sentence. My mom got so many notes sent home about it. She used to keep them in this big yellow folder in the kitchen drawer. That drawer was so full of junk, honestly. It had all these old takeout menus, and half of the places aren't even open anymore. Like that Chinese place down the street? They closed last year and turned into a vape shop. Which is crazy because there's literally another vape shop right across the street from it. How many do we really need? I tried one of those disposable ones once, the blue razz flavor, and it made me cough so bad. I felt like my lungs were on fire. My friend Sarah smokes them all the time, though. She goes through like two a week. She works at the mall, at that pretzel place. Have you had those? The cinnamon sugar ones are the best, especially when they're fresh out of the oven. But yeah, what did you ask me? Oh, school! Yeah, I couldn't sit still at all. Always getting in trouble for it.",
